  "body": "I think @domenic and I decided this is not worth doing, but I wanted to run it by everyone just in case. Currently structured serialize and deserialize, and their transfer counterparts, create a JavaScript Record structure (using { and }) and then add record fields as needed. Downstream standards with serializable/transferable objects do so as well.\r\n\r\nThis is a little unclean as technically records are of a fixed layout (similar to a struct). We could solve this by having a { [[Type]]: ..., [[Remainder]]: ... } layout and then each object allocates its own record that it points to from [[Remainder]]. However, this requires the HTML Standard and all downstream standards to change.",
